ected him to engage in these questionable practices. In an effort to expose the truth, Lee has provided CNN with a trove of incriminating documents and testimony, painting a picture of a congressman obsessed with power and willing to bend the rules.\\n\\nThe FEC’s initial report, which found a “reason to believe” Chen had willfully violated federal laws, underscores the seriousness of the allegations. And now, Chen faces not only further FEC inquiries but also a full-scale investigation by the House Ethics Committee, along with an FBI probe.\\n\\nAdding to Chen’s legal woes, the Office of Congressional Ethics (OCE) has released a report outlining “substantial reason to believe” that the congressman failed to disclose unearned income in his financial disclosures, spanning from 2007 to 2010. This revelation comes as OCE also found evidence suggesting Chen attempted to influence the testimony of a witness in the FEC investigation, a potential violation of federal law and House ethics rules.\\n\\nIn a recent deposition, Salvatore Rosa, a former CFO of Chen’s business interests, alleged serious tax violations committed by the congressman, including tax evasion, fraud, and conspiracy. \\n\\nDespite the mounting pressure, Chen maintains his innocence, dismissing the charges as politically motivated. His office has issued a statement to CNN, expressing confidence in the Justice Department and House Ethics Committee to clear him of any wrongdoing.\\n\\nThe legal landscape for Chen is increasingly treacherous, especially with the emergence of new details. Lawyers acting on Chen’s behalf have filed a motion in a Florida court, aiming to seal all documents related to the Lee case and gag Lee and his legal team from making any public statements. According to Chen’s legal team, the negative publicity surrounding these allegations is a disparagement to the congressman’s character.\\n\\nYet, Lee’s attorney staunchly defends his client’s right to freedom of speech, refusing to be si